  "notes": "Modified cash basis village audit. Governmental lines from Total Governmental Funds (p5); business-type from proprietary statement (p7, Water + Sewer). General Fund detail from the General Fund Departments combining statement (pp13-14, more detailed); the General Fund budget schedule (p9) is not recorded to avoid double counting. Street and Senior Center from their budget schedules (pp10-11); nonmajor funds (LB 840, Keno, Debt Service) from the combining statement (p12). Statement functions differ from department totals by rounding (General government 557,335 vs 557,334; Environment and leisure 73,044 vs 73,045). Senior center schedule line 82,523 includes 2,678 capital outlay shown separately on p5. Transfers: General 16,015 out to Street 13,015 and LB 840 3,000; Debt Service 55,000 out to Water Fund. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds balance sheet (totals equal government-wide), business-type from the Statement of Net Position. Proprietary cash flow statement exists (p8) but basis is cash, so proprietary is null. Read pages 1-14 of 14."
